    "result_text": "The full test suite is a single test class (`AcceptanceTest`) with 2 tests, and both pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` derived field on the owner resource, following the existing Spring/MapStruct conventions used for the other derived owner fields (`membershipLevel`, `locality`, `ageBand`, etc.).\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added the read-only `ownerSegment` string property to the `Owner` schema (after `ageBand`), documenting the `<TIER>_<AREA>` format and its four possible values. The OpenAPI generator produces the corresponding `OwnerDto` getter/setter.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerSegmentResolver.java`** (new) \u2014 A resolver class (mirroring `LocalityResolver`/`MembershipLevelResolver`) that:\n   - Sets TIER to `PREMIUM` when `MembershipLevelResolver.deriveMembershipLevel(owner) >= 3`, else `STANDARD`.\n   - Sets AREA to `METRO` when the derived locality matches a known `Region` (NSW/VIC/QLD), else `REGIONAL`.\n   - Returns `<TIER>_<AREA>`.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added the `@Mapping` for `ownerSegment` delegating to the new resolver.\n\nThe resolver reuses the existing `MembershipLevelResolver`, `LocalityResolver`, and `Region` types so the tier/area rules stay consistent with how `membershipLevel` and `locality` are already computed.",
